/**

\page page_third-party_hdf5 HDF5 and NetCDF

\tableofcontents

## HDF5

Peano writes its own mesh files without HDF5 and reads only input formats that work without it. An
application needs HDF5 to write HDF5 files or to use an extension that requires HDF5. The CMake
option PEANO_WITH_HDF5 switches the HDF5 support on. It is ON by default:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cmake .. -DPEANO_WITH_HDF5=ON
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

CMake finds HDF5 with find_package(HDF5 COMPONENTS C) and links the target HDF5::HDF5. This target
provides the include directories and the libraries. For an HDF5 installation in a non-standard
location, set the environment variable or the CMake hint HDF5_ROOT.

Peano uses the C interface of HDF5 only. If PEANO_WITH_HDF5 is ON and CMake cannot find an HDF5
installation, the build prints a warning and continues without HDF5 support. The HDF5 installation
must support parallel I/O.

## NetCDF

Some applications need NetCDF. The CMake option PEANO_WITH_NETCDF switches the NetCDF support on.
It is ON by default:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cmake .. -DPEANO_WITH_NETCDF=ON
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

cmake/FindPeanoNetCDF.cmake searches the paths of the pkg-config module netcdf and the paths in the
environment variables below. For a NetCDF installation in a non-standard location, set these
variables before CMake runs:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
export NETCDF_DIR=/path/to/netcdf            # prefix containing include/ and lib/
# or, more specifically:
export NETCDF_INCLUDE_DIR=/path/to/netcdf/include
export NETCDF_LIB_DIR=/path/to/netcdf/lib
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If PEANO_WITH_NETCDF is ON and CMake cannot find a NetCDF installation, the build prints a warning and
continues without NetCDF support. The NetCDF installation must write NetCDF-4 files through HDF5
and support parallel I/O.

*/
